{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","hash":"3ec9a0cbe6ddeb9ae3ee535339ccea7f727cee1b57ab7ec0c3e1c67217d60449","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018cUhkwCbUjUd7pNRDCHeVm","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-distill-fix && git add -A && git -c commit.gpgsign=false commit -q -F - <<'MSG'\nfix(watch,distill): stop the daemon racing its own worker, and stop paying twice for merged sessions\n\nThree defects in the distill pipeline, all of which ship in the release.\n\nCOR-2175 — the daemon blocked itself.\n\nThe watch tick queued long-term reconciliation, launched `memory worker\n--once` DETACHED, then ran a refresh needing the same brain write.lock. The\nworker starts first and holds it 11-16s; refresh's timeout is shorter. The\ntick logged brain_locked, skipped ALL agent work including distill, and did\nnot advance its cursor. 368 of 369 observed brain_locked failures followed a\nreconciliation queued in the same tick, and any repo with an active session\nhas a changed transcript on nearly every tick -- so that repo's daemon distill\neffectively never ran.\n\nThe watch tick now WAITS for the worker it spawned. Every other caller keeps\nthe detached launch: notify and the session-end hook are done once the work is\nqueued, and making them block on a 16s worker would slow a fast path for no\nbenefit. The wait costs a background tick the worker's runtime, which is the\nright trade on a 5m interval -- a tick that takes 16s longer and then distills\nbeats one that returns fast having done nothing.\n\nThe issue offered \"skip the worker and let refresh's consolidation do the\nwork\" as the cheaper option. refresh.go contains no consolidation at all, so\nthat would have silently dropped it. Checked before choosing.\n\nCOR-2177 — distill re-paid for every branch copy.\n\nThe cache is keyed branch/session, and session export deliberately copies a\nmerged feature-branch session onto the default branch. Every copy was a cache\nmiss with zero chunk reuse, so the same transcript went back to the agent once\nper branch. Measured on agent-insights: 69 \"sessions\" were 41 unique, 19 on\nmore than one branch, --dry-run reporting 209 of 209 chunks uncached.\n\nReuse is now content-addressed across every branch carrying the session, which\nis sound because the hashes ARE content hashes: an identical chunk has already\nbeen through the agent and its facts are already in the store, whichever branch\npaid. Chunking is prefix-stable, so a copied transcript resolves almost\nentirely from the union.\n\nThe matcher is segment-exact, deliberately. A substring match would let one\nsession's hashes mask another's, and a chunk wrongly believed distilled is a\nchunk whose facts never get written -- worse than paying twice. Negative\ncontrols cover \"abc\" vs \"abcdef\" and a branch named like a session.\n\nCOR-2176 — watch.log could not be read.\n\nBare `[watch] ...` lines, no clock, and on a workspace fan-out no way to tell\nwhich repo a line was about. Diagnosing 2175 meant correlating two lines and\nGUESSING they were the same tick on the same repo, which only worked because\none repo dominated that log. Stamped at the WRITER, so a line added later\ncannot forget it, and per line rather than per write so a two-line tick does\nnot leave its second line unattributed.\n\nVerified by weakening, four guards:\n  - reverting the watch tick to the detached launch       -> red\n  - removing the cross-branch half of the reuse decision  -> red\n  - making the session matcher a substring                -> red\n  - blanking the log stamp                                -> red\n\nOne of those only became a real guard after a correction: the first chunk-reuse\ntest asserted the helper directly and stayed GREEN when the call site was\nchanged to ignore it -- the same shape as the bug. The decision is now\ndistillChunksAlreadyDone, a value the loop calls, and the test drives that.\n\nFull internal/cli suite green, every other package green, go vet ./... clean.\nMSG\ngit push -u origin fix/distill-pipeline 2>&1 | grep -viE \"^remote:|vulnerab|dependabot|^\\[entire\\]|cannot lock|another git\" | tail -2","description":"Commit and push the distill pipeline fixes"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
