{"parentUuid":"d4d49e14-f179-4e61-94b1-99d8d47d2a02","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14958095 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"84c0902d-b353-4f22-90d1-7a265619532d","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:55:22.556Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14958095 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"60a744a6-1b89-494f-a7de-f94ff9566958","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-distill-fix","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.301","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"84c0902d-b353-4f22-90d1-7a265619532d","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_018cUhkwCbUjUd7pNRDCHeVm","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"5360bc13-3fd8-48f0-aa79-0cf035b3bc64","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:55:38.792Z","session_id":"60a744a6-1b89-494f-a7de-f94ff9566958","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-distill-fix","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.301","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"5360bc13-3fd8-48f0-aa79-0cf035b3bc64","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgG8NCkVS3HunxmbY9Rgy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011SrQDqSWRUTbZbGTH41Xed","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"gh pr create --repo entireio/entire-brain --base main --head fix/distill-pipeline --title \"fix(watch,distill): stop the daemon racing its own worker, and stop paying twice for merged sessions\" --body-file - <<'BODY' 2>&1 | tail -2\nThree defects in the distill pipeline, all of which would ship in tonight's release. Closes **COR-2175**, **COR-2177**, **COR-2176**.\n\n## COR-2175 — the daemon blocked itself 🔴\n\nThe watch tick queued long-term reconciliation, launched `memory worker --once` **detached**, then ran a refresh needing the same brain `write.lock`. The worker starts first and holds it 11–16s; refresh's timeout is shorter. The tick logged `brain_locked`, **skipped all agent work including distill**, and did not advance its cursor.\n\n**368 of 369** observed `brain_locked` failures followed a reconciliation queued in the same tick. Any repo with an active session has a changed transcript on nearly every tick — so that repo's daemon distill effectively never ran.\n\nThe watch tick now **waits** for the worker it spawned. Every other caller keeps the detached launch: notify and the session-end hook are done once the work is queued, and blocking them on a 16s worker would slow a fast path for nothing. The wait costs a background tick the worker's runtime — the right trade on a 5m interval.\n\n> The issue offered a cheaper option: *\"skip the worker and let refresh's consolidation do the work.\"* **`refresh.go` contains no consolidation at all**, so that would have silently dropped it. Checked before choosing.\n\n## COR-2177 — distill re-paid for every branch copy 🔴\n\nThe cache is keyed `branch/session`, and session export **deliberately** copies a merged feature-branch session onto the default branch. Every copy was a cache miss with zero chunk reuse, so the same transcript went back to the agent once per branch.\n\nMeasured on `agent-insights`: 69 \"sessions\" were **41 unique**, 19 on more than one branch, `--dry-run` reporting **209 of 209 chunks uncached**.\n\nReuse is now content-addressed across every branch carrying the session. That's sound because the hashes *are* content hashes — an identical chunk has already been through the agent and its facts are already in the store, whichever branch paid. Chunking is prefix-stable, so a copied transcript resolves almost entirely from the union.\n\nThe matcher is **segment-exact**, deliberately. A substring match would let one session's hashes mask another's, and *a chunk wrongly believed distilled is a chunk whose facts never get written* — worse than paying twice. Negative controls cover `abc` vs `abcdef`, and a branch named like a session.\n\n## COR-2176 — watch.log could not be read 🟡\n\nBare `[watch] …` lines: no clock, and on a workspace fan-out no way to tell which repo a line was about. Diagnosing 2175 meant correlating two lines and *guessing* they were the same tick on the same repo — which only worked because one repo dominated that log.\n\nStamped at the **writer**, so a line added later cannot forget it, and **per line** rather than per write so a two-line tick doesn't leave its second line unattributed.\n\n## Verification\n\nVerified by weakening — four guards, each reverted individually:\n\n| weakening | result |\n|---|---|\n| watch tick back to the detached launch | **red** |\n| cross-branch half removed from the reuse decision | **red** |\n| session matcher made a substring | **red** |\n| log stamp blanked | **red** |\n\nOne only became a real guard after a correction: the first chunk-reuse test asserted the helper directly and stayed **green** when the call site was changed to ignore it — the same shape as the bug. The decision is now `distillChunksAlreadyDone`, a value the loop calls, and the test drives that.\n\nFull `internal/cli` suite green, every other package green, `go vet ./...` clean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nBODY","description":"Open the PR","timeout":300000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1566,"cache_read_input_tokens":864288,"output_tokens":1462,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1566,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1462,"cache_read_input_tokens":864288,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1566,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1566},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_011SrQDqSWRUTbZbGTH41Xed":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-distill-fix && gh pr create --repo entireio/entire-brain --base main --head fix/distill-pipeline --title \"fix(watch,distill): stop the daemon racing its own worker, and stop paying twice for merged sessions\" --body-file - <<'BODY' 2>&1 | tail -2\nThree defects in the distill pipeline, all of which would ship in tonight's release. Closes **COR-2175**, **COR-2177**, **COR-2176**.\n\n## COR-2175 — the daemon blocked itself 🔴\n\nThe watch tick queued long-term reconciliation, launched `memory worker --once` **detached**, then ran a refresh needing the same brain `write.lock`. The worker starts first and holds it 11–16s; refresh's timeout is shorter. The tick logged `brain_locked`, **skipped all agent work including distill**, and did not advance its cursor.\n\n**368 of 369** observed `brain_locked` failures followed a reconciliation queued in the same tick. Any repo with an active session has a changed transcript on nearly every tick — so that repo's daemon distill effectively never ran.\n\nThe watch tick now **waits** for the worker it spawned. Every other caller keeps the detached launch: notify and the session-end hook are done once the work is queued, and blocking them on a 16s worker would slow a fast path for nothing. The wait costs a background tick the worker's runtime — the right trade on a 5m interval.\n\n> The issue offered a cheaper option: *\"skip the worker and let refresh's consolidation do the work.\"* **`refresh.go` contains no consolidation at all**, so that would have silently dropped it. Checked before choosing.\n\n## COR-2177 — distill re-paid for every branch copy 🔴\n\nThe cache is keyed `branch/session`, and session export **deliberately** copies a merged feature-branch session onto the default branch. Every copy was a cache miss with zero chunk reuse, so the same transcript went back to the agent once per branch.\n\nMeasured on `agent-insights`: 69 \"sessions\" were **41 unique**, 19 on more than one branch, `--dry-run` reporting **209 of 209 chunks uncached**.\n\nReuse is now content-addressed across every branch carrying the session. That's sound because the hashes *are* content hashes — an identical chunk has already been through the agent and its facts are already in the store, whichever branch paid. Chunking is prefix-stable, so a copied transcript resolves almost entirely from the union.\n\nThe matcher is **segment-exact**, deliberately. A substring match would let one session's hashes mask another's, and *a chunk wrongly believed distilled is a chunk whose facts never get written* — worse than paying twice. Negative controls cover `abc` vs `abcdef`, and a branch named like a session.\n\n## COR-2176 — watch.log could not be read 🟡\n\nBare `[watch] …` lines: no clock, and on a workspace fan-out no way to tell which repo a line was about. Diagnosing 2175 meant correlating two lines and *guessing* they were the same tick on the same repo — which only worked because one repo dominated that log.\n\nStamped at the **writer**, so a line added later cannot forget it, and **per line** rather than per write so a two-line tick doesn't leave its second line unattributed.\n\n## Verification\n\nVerified by weakening — four guards, each reverted individually:\n\n| weakening | result |\n|---|---|\n| watch tick back to the detached launch | **red** |\n| cross-branch half removed from the reuse decision | **red** |\n| session matcher made a substring | **red** |\n| log stamp blanked | **red** |\n\nOne only became a real guard after a correction: the first chunk-reuse test asserted the helper directly and stayed **green** when the call site was changed to ignore it — the same shape as the bug. The decision is now `distillChunksAlreadyDone`, a value the loop calls, and the test drives that.\n\nFull `internal/cli` suite green, every other package green, `go vet ./...` clean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nBODY","description":"Open the PR","timeout":300000}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_011SrQDqSWRUTbZbGTH41Xed":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-distill-fix"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"90d83820-7e8f-41bb-b2a3-6841d04bf354","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgG8NBZoPc1K1nPpzwm8k","requestRef":"57b351b7-4be8-40d7-8620-07a2f435df83","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"4f748470-8fea-423b-a7dc-f7f8092f93a8","timestamp":"2026-10-21T21:55:38.790Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"60a744a6-1b89-494f-a7de-f94ff9566958","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-distill-fix","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.301","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
